    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that overall investment from China into AI is \nconsiderably lower than it is here in America.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1083040,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, if this is really a race, spending alone isn't \ngoing to be the deciding factor. Now, to be clear,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1088720,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "China is not exactly a model citizen of any of \nthis. And there is plenty to criticize about how  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1094400,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these laws actually get applied. Enforcement is \nreal, but selective and politically motivated,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1099680,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with rules getting deployed against companies \nthat fall out of favor and conveniently ignored  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1104080,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for companies that haven't. Many provisions are \nwritten vaguely enough that they can really only  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1109280,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be enforced when the party feels like enforcing \nthem. And most of the financial penalties by  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1114080,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tech company standards are small enough to be \npriced in as a cost of doing business rather  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1118160,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than treated as a serious deterrent. So no, China \nis very obviously not running a civics class on AI  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1124960,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ethics here. A lot of these rules are functionally \nabout state control of information rather than  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1129600,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "user safety in any meaningful sense. But that is \nsort of the point. China is strongarmming its tech  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1136000,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sector into developing AI in a way that for better \nor worse forwards the interests of the state.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1141840,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "America is told that the way to beat this is to \nlet its tech sector do whatever they want in the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1146640,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vague hope that private interest and geopolitical \ninterest align. From the market's point of view,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1151520,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is already working exactly as intended. \nAnd if you want further proof of that,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1155920,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "go watch this video next to find out how OpenAI's \nproblems are already becoming our problems.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1161920,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And don't forget to like and subscribe \nto keep on learning how money works."
    } ]
  } ]
}
